WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.320
I wanna make sure we talk about

00:00:01.320 --> 00:00:06.320
what you're up to now. Because
this project is so cool.

00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:11.360
It's spelled, it's
seasons, but it's S Z N Z.

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:14.610
Yeah. So it's called SZNZ

00:00:14.610 --> 00:00:18.390
and there's Spring,
Summer, Autumn, and Winter.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:20.640
And each one comes out

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.340
on the first day of its respective season.

00:00:23.340 --> 00:00:26.340
And together they kind of all add up to a

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.500
something that feels like a hole.

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:33.150
And each album has a primary emotion.

00:00:33.150 --> 00:00:36.180
Spring is optimistic,

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:37.480
Summer is angry

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:41.850
Autumn is anxious, Winter is sad.

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:44.880
Each album has a primary genre.

00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:47.490
So, Spring is supposed
to sound kind of like

00:00:47.490 --> 00:00:48.603
Island in the Sun.

00:00:49.590 --> 00:00:53.400
Summer is supposed to sound
like alternative nineties rock.

00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:56.460
And Autumn, which is about to come out

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.270
is like dance rock, Franz
Ferdinand, is that sort of thing.

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:04.260
And nineties, sorry, Winter
is like 90 singer songwriter,

00:01:04.260 --> 00:01:05.580
Elliot Smith, that kind of thing.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:06.413
Wow?

00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:07.723
That is such a great idea.

00:01:07.723 --> 00:01:08.556
That's amazing.

00:01:08.556 --> 00:01:09.900
Oh wow, thanks.
That's an amazing idea.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:10.930
No, it really, I mean.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.784
No one's ever said that.

00:01:12.784 --> 00:01:13.800
What? No one's said that?

00:01:13.800 --> 00:01:15.660
The three of us just all at the same time,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:16.920
and we don't agree on anything.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:17.753
No.

00:01:17.753 --> 00:01:19.860
But it's so funny how
everyone in the room just now,

00:01:19.860 --> 00:01:20.820
you know, Matt and Sona,

00:01:20.820 --> 00:01:22.320
and all of us are just like,

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.920
Oh, that's just awesome.
What a great idea.

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:26.880
That really is.

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.200
Now what inspired you?

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.965
Well, it all started with Dropbox because,

00:01:31.965 --> 00:01:32.798
What?

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:36.750
Beethoven said the same thing.

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.750
(everyone laughing)

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.120
I just, every day, I just write

00:01:45.120 --> 00:01:47.760
and I don't think about
where a song is gonna go.

00:01:47.760 --> 00:01:48.593
I don't, I don't.

00:01:48.593 --> 00:01:51.060
It's just whatever sounds
cool to me in the moment.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:52.500
But because of Dropbox,

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:54.690
I would just sort them into
these different folders

00:01:54.690 --> 00:01:57.000
and, Well, this sounds
kind of like Dance Rock,

00:01:57.000 --> 00:01:58.020
so I'll put it in this folder,

00:01:58.020 --> 00:02:00.450
or this one sounds like
nineties singer song writer.

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:01.410
I'll put it over here.

00:02:01.410 --> 00:02:03.090
And everything was just all nice

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:05.493
and neatly sorted and
everything had a home.

00:02:06.360 --> 00:02:08.370
And I didn't have to worry about,

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.550
well, we're making this
kind of album this year,

00:02:11.550 --> 00:02:13.830
so everything has to
fit a particular sound.

00:02:13.830 --> 00:02:17.133
It just went to whatever
folder it actually belonged in.

00:02:18.090 --> 00:02:19.980
And then I started thinking like,

00:02:19.980 --> 00:02:21.330
well, what can I do with all this?

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:22.500
How can I tie it together?

00:02:22.500 --> 00:02:24.834
Or should I make four
different albums or what?

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:28.440
And somehow I remembered
of all these four seasons

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.390
and well there's four seasons

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:32.700
and yeah, maybe we can
kind of tie it together

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:33.753
under that umbrella.

00:02:34.890 --> 00:02:39.890
And so you released one, is
the whole project done now,

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:42.564
and you're just waiting to
release them in time or no?

00:02:42.564 --> 00:02:44.400
We're kind of it in real time.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.700
So like, we're like, we
just turned in Autumn

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.170
and it's gonna come out obviously,

00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:51.780
what is it, September 21st?

00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:53.580
Yeah. So it's a very last minute.

00:02:53.580 --> 00:02:57.030
And for the fans, it's been
fun to watch it all happen

00:02:57.030 --> 00:02:58.560
in real time.

00:02:58.560 --> 00:03:01.410
Watch Weezer scramble
to meet the deadlines.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.880
Did you find that you were angry

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.230
when you were making Summer?

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:06.947
I was definitely anxious
when I was making Autumn.

00:03:06.947 --> 00:03:08.310
(everyone laughing)

00:03:08.310 --> 00:03:09.780
No. Yeah, I did.

00:03:09.780 --> 00:03:14.220
I did feel, maybe I just noticing it

00:03:14.220 --> 00:03:16.811
because it was on my mind, but I have felt

00:03:16.811 --> 00:03:20.520
those emotions as I was making each album.

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:21.870
I'm a little worried about Winter now.

00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:22.950
Yeah. You're gonna get sad.

00:03:22.950 --> 00:03:24.178
Yeah.

00:03:24.178 --> 00:03:25.380
Yeah. We're just starting that one now.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.840
I could come by with
like an ice cream cake.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:28.786
Oh no.

00:03:28.786 --> 00:03:29.619
What?

00:03:29.619 --> 00:03:30.720
But I need to be sad.

00:03:30.720 --> 00:03:31.890
Yeah.

00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:32.723
With an ice cream cake.

00:03:32.723 --> 00:03:33.990
Well, it's not gonna be a good,

00:03:33.990 --> 00:03:34.823
Here's the thing,

00:03:34.823 --> 00:03:36.474
it's not gonna be a good ice cream cake.

00:03:36.474 --> 00:03:37.932
Oh, okay.

00:03:37.932 --> 00:03:38.765
Yeah.

00:03:38.765 --> 00:03:39.598
It'll just make him more sad.

00:03:39.598 --> 00:03:42.003
Yeah. And it's gonna
say, I hate you on it.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.340
That's a terrible idea.

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.980
Well, it's gonna make him sad.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:48.810
He didn't let me finish.

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:49.980
God, these guys jump in

00:03:49.980 --> 00:03:52.470
whenever I think I have
a really good idea.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.670
They totally screw with me.

00:03:53.670 --> 00:03:54.543
It's not right.

